Subject: [PATCH] minimum arm64: ship R AppMarket on the image

R AppMarket (browse and install every app in each pkgman repository it
knows about, from a window) used to be something a fresh guest had to
`pkgman install` by hand before it could use it to install anything
else -- the one app a minimal image most needs already on it, since
everything else in RENKU Apps is reached through it. Baked into the
image the same way curl/gzip/tar/wget and openssh already are: the
hpkg is in ../packages/, and add-media-arm64.sh copies it into the
generated directory's download/.

The copy in ../packages/ says vendor "Haiku Project", not "RENKU":
this build's own local HaikuPorts-info repository (built from
everything in download/) refuses a package whose vendor differs from
the rest of it, same as 0012's curl/wget note already explains. It is
rebuilt from the same recipe as the "RENKU" one published live on
pkgman.rainygirl.com, just with REPO_VENDOR set to "Haiku Project" for
this one copy -- same binary, different vendor metadata only.

diff -ru a/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles b/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles
--- a/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles	2026-10-09 13:01:32.000000000 +0000
+++ b/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles	2026-10-12 19:55:29.000000000 +0000
@@ -240,6 +240,15 @@
 					openssh
 					;
 			}
+
+			# R AppMarket: so pkgman install's own GUI is on the image from
+			# first boot instead of needing itself installed by hand first.
+			# Published in RENKU Apps, like curl/gzip/tar/wget above.
+			if $(TARGET_PACKAGING_ARCH) = arm64 {
+				AddHaikuImageSystemPackages
+					rappmarket
+					;
+			}
 		}

 		case "test-*" : {
diff -ru a/build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64 b/build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64
--- a/build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64	2026-10-09 13:01:32.000000000 +0000
+++ b/build/jam/repositories/HaikuPorts/arm64	2026-10-12 19:55:42.000000000 +0000
@@ -72,6 +72,8 @@
 	sqlite3-3.50.4-1
 	webpositive-r1~beta6_hrev99000_dirty-1
 	openssh-10.4p1-1
+	# R AppMarket -- published in RENKU Apps, same as curl/gzip/tar/wget above.
+	rappmarket-1.0.0-4
 	:
 	# source packages
 	bash
